---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import SourceList from '../../../components/SourceList.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';
import CombatFlow from '../../../components/CombatFlow.astro';
import CombatScreenshot from '../../../components/CombatScreenshot.astro';
import StatusEffectsFieldGuide from '../../../components/StatusEffectsFieldGuide.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import { sourceUrls } from '../../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Signal Skills & Status Effects Guide';
const description = 'Learn how to trigger Signal Skills in DragonSword Awakening, diagnose missing prompts, and match Status Ailments to the exact Signal Skill conditions shown in your current build.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/guides/combat-system/';
const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: title,
  description,
  mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
  datePublished: '2026-08-08',
  dateModified: '2026-09-01',
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' },
};
const sources = [{
  label: 'Official Steam store page',
  href: sourceUrls.steam,
  note: 'describes 19 Heroes, Status Ailments, Active Skills, Signal Skills and Switching Signals.',
}];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Signal Skills' }]} />
    <article>
      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Guide · Read the signal</p>
        <h1>DragonSword Awakening Signal Skills & Status Effects Guide</h1>
        <LastVerified date="September 1, 2026" />
      </header>

      <QuickAnswer title="Match the exact condition, then wait for the prompt.">
        <p>Use an Active Skill to apply the Status Ailment named by another Hero’s Signal Skill. Check any additional condition written in the current skill description, then activate the Signal or switch when its prompt appears.</p>
      </QuickAnswer>

      <div class="article-body">
        <SectionHeader
          title="How to Trigger Signal Skills in DragonSword Awakening"
          description="Treat every handoff as an exact condition check, not a fixed timer or a generic character swap."
        />
        <CombatFlow />
        <CombatScreenshot
          src="/media/combat-system/signal-condition-handoff.jpg"
          alt="DragonSword Awakening combat HUD showing a three-Hero party, enemy status icons and a Tag Combo prompt"
          caption="Read the party order, enemy condition row and available teammate prompt as one handoff state."
        />

        <h2>1. Start with the receiving Signal Skill</h2>
        <p>Read the Signal Skill first and note the status or combat condition it requires. This gives you a concrete setup target before you spend an Active Skill.</p>

        <h2>2. Apply the required Status Ailment</h2>
        <p>Use a Hero whose Active Skill names that condition. A different status may still be useful, but it will not satisfy a Signal that asks for something else.</p>

        <h2>3. Check additional conditions</h2>
        <p>A matching status may be only part of the requirement. Check the current skill text, the target’s Super Armor or Break state, and whether the intended Signal is available before expecting a prompt.</p>
        <CombatScreenshot
          src="/media/combat-system/status-row-and-team-prompt.jpg"
          alt="DragonSword Awakening boss battle HUD showing stacked enemy status icons and an available teammate prompt"
          caption="Several enemy conditions can be visible at once, so match the receiving Signal to the exact condition it names."
        />

        <h2>4. Activate the prompt or switch</h2>
        <p>When the matching Signal window appears, activate it or bring in the Hero who can continue the chain. If no prompt appears, return to the exact trigger description instead of repeating the same swap.</p>
        <CombatScreenshot
          src="/media/combat-system/airborne-signal-window.jpg"
          alt="DragonSword Awakening aerial combat showing an enemy status icon and an available Tag Combo prompt"
          caption="Use the visible prompt as the action cue; the screenshot illustrates timing, not a universal rotation."
        />

        <StatusEffectsFieldGuide />
        <AdsterraNativeBanner />

        <h2>Why team order matters</h2>
        <p>A useful team has readable handoffs: one Hero creates a condition, the next Hero owns a matching Signal, and the third can continue from the state that follows.</p>

        <h2>Setup, connector, payoff</h2>
        <p>This is planning language, not an official class system. Use it to check whether each team slot can create or answer a condition without presenting one rotation as a universal meta.</p>
      </div>

      <SourceList sources={sources} />
      <RelatedGuides links={[{ label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Teams', href: '/teams/' }, { label: 'Characters', href: '/characters/' }]} />
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; }
  .article-header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-light); font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1, h2 { line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .7rem; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); }
  h2 { margin: 2.8rem 0 .75rem; font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .article-body { max-width: 760px; }
  .article-body p { color: var(--muted-strong); }
</style>
